CSE 598 - Lab #1 (PART 1)
Asynchronous FIFO

DESCRIPTION
-----------
This project implements a parameterized asynchronous FIFO in SystemVerilog.

The FIFO uses separate read and write clock domains, Gray-code pointers,
two-flip-flop synchronizers for clock-domain crossing, and status flags
for full, empty, almost_full, and almost_empty.

DEPTH must be a power of two. async_fifo derives ADDR_WIDTH as $clog2(DEPTH)
and fifo_mem builds 1<<ADDR_WIDTH entries, so a DEPTH of 12 silently becomes a
FIFO of 16. The almost_full and almost_empty thresholds, (3*DEPTH)/4 and
DEPTH/4, are integer divisions and are exact only for powers of two as well.


FILES
-----
fifo_if.sv
    SystemVerilog interface and modport used by the FIFO memory.

fifo_mem.sv
    FIFO memory/register array.

sync_r2w.sv
    Synchronizes the read pointer into the write clock domain.

sync_w2r.sv
    Synchronizes the write pointer into the read clock domain.

fifo_rptr.sv
    Read pointer, read address, empty, and almost_empty logic.

fifo_wptr.sv
    Write pointer, write address, full, and almost_full logic.

async_fifo.sv
    Top-level asynchronous FIFO connecting all internal blocks.

tb_async_fifo.sv
    SystemVerilog testbench containing the three verification scenarios.

Makefile
    Commands for compilation, simulation, Verdi, and cleanup.

env.cshrc
    Synopsys tool paths and licence settings, csh syntax.

env.sh
    The same settings in bash syntax. Use this one on Apporto.


SETUP
-----
Change into this directory first, then load the course environment.

The Apporto default shell is bash, so use env.sh:

    source env.sh

env.cshrc is the csh version of the same thing. It uses setenv, so sourcing it
from bash prints "setenv: command not found" for every line and leaves VCS off
the PATH. Use it only from csh or tcsh:

    source env.cshrc

Check it took effect before compiling:

    which vcs


COMPILATION
-----------
Compile the design and testbench using:

    make compile

This creates the VCS executable named simv.


TESTS
-----
Test 1 - Empty -> Full -> Empty:

    do it with: make test1

Test 2 - almost_full and almost_empty flags:

    do it with: make test2

Test 3 - Simultaneous read/write using different clock frequencies:

    do it with: make test3

All tests use the same compiled simv executable.


WAVEFORMS
---------
Each simulation creates a novas.fsdb waveform database.

To open the most recently generated waveform in Verdi:

    make verdi
If you want to open the other ones, make sure to simulate them first and them open the waveforms.


CLEANUP
-------
To remove tool-generated simulation files:

    make clean

The clean target does not remove the SystemVerilog source files,
Makefile, or README. They are important for the submission of the Lab's part 1.
